        "original_id": "6bf7afdf-0d90-5ad0-84f7-e64d0940bbc8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Rice, Leslie Marmon Silko, Elton John, Kenneth Lincoln\n- Works: “Can You Feel the Love Tonight”, The Lion King\n- Organizations: Disney\n- Concepts: Native American Renaissance\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Rice was born on 10 November 1944 and is an English author and lyricist.\n- Leslie Marmon Silko was born on March 5, 1948, is a Laguna Pueblo writer, and is considered a key figure in the First Wave of the Native American Renaissance identified by literary critic Kenneth Lincoln.\n- Disney released the animated film The Lion King in 1994.\n- “Can You Feel the Love Tonight” is a song from Disney’s 1994 animated film The Lion King.\n- Elton John composed “Can You Feel the Love Tonight,” and Tim Rice wrote its lyrics.\n- Tim Rice has won Academy, Golden Globe, Tony, and Grammy Awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
